# Outline knowledge — YT short creator

Collection aligned with Plane **YTSC** (`yt-short-creator`).
LAN `http://10.100.30.91:3000` · UI `https://outline.marcatos.ddns.net` · IdP Authentik.

Follow the same Outline operating rules as all personal projects under `Documents/Projects` (user rule `outline-personal-projects`).

## Document set (use all of these — not only STATUS/DECISIONS)

| Document | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Overview** | Map of this collection and how to read it |
| **STATUS** | Live facts only — short, current |
| **DECISIONS** | Append-only ADRs with accepted and rejected options |
| **Features** | Feature catalog with status and links |
| **Specs** | Requirements / acceptance criteria index |
| **Implementation** | How it is built and verified |
| **Options** | Alternatives explored (accepted, rejected, deferred) |

## Canonical owners

| Artefact | Owner |
|---|---|
| Live facts | Outline **STATUS** |
| Locked choices (+ rejected options) | Outline **DECISIONS** (append at top) + full **ADR …** docs |
| Explored alternatives | Outline **Options** |
| Feature catalog | Outline **Features** |
| Requirements | Outline **Specs** / `Spec: …` |
| How built / verified | Outline **Implementation** |
| Technical debt | Outline **Technical debt** (when the project tracks TD) |
| Research / runbooks | Outline `Research: …` / `Runbook: …` |
| Work + session notes | Plane work items + comments |
| Changelog | conventional commits |
| Code | git |

## Agent workflow

1. **Session start:** list open Plane items; read **STATUS**; skim **Features** if changing product behaviour.
2. **New capability:** row in **Features** → requirements in **Specs** (or `Spec: …`) → Plane work item before coding.
3. **Design choice:** capture alternatives in **Options**; when locking, append **DECISIONS** with **Accepted / Rejected / Deferred**. Create a full **ADR …** (or equivalent) Outline document when the choice is architectural.
4. **After ship:** update **Implementation** + **STATUS** facts; set Feature status; comment the Plane issue.
5. Keep **STATUS** short. Never put secrets on Outline. Do not treat git STATUS/DECISIONS as live.

## Repo mirroring (mandatory)

If Outline cites an ADR, research note, technical-debt item, acceptance checklist, playbook, or other repo doc, the **full body must exist on Outline** in this collection (e.g. `ADR 0011 — …`, `Research: …`, `Technical debt`). Do **not** leave “see `docs/adr/….md`” (or similar git paths) as the only source. When you add or change such a doc in git, upsert the Outline document in the **same session**.

## Cross-links (mandatory)

When updating Outline docs, use real internal links (`[Title](/doc/…-urlId)` from the Outline API `url` field), not bare titles alone. Hub pages (**Overview**, **STATUS**, **DECISIONS**, **Features**, **Specs**, **Implementation**, **Options**, **ADRs**) must link to the docs they reference; Specs/ADRs/Runbooks should link back to Features / DECISIONS / STATUS as relevant.

